cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CCRP DataSet, please cite this dataset and its two independent companion papers (see preferred-citation and references)."
title: "Chinese Character Riddle Probes Dataset (CCRP DataSet)"
type: dataset
# The dataset content version is 0.1 and does not change between patch
# releases. v0.1.1 is a documentation-only repository patch (see CHANGELOG.md).
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
license:
  - CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - name: "Spring Buds Data Source Inc."
    alias: "春芽数源"
    country: CN
abstract: >-
  A 100-character Chinese character riddle dataset for behavioral structural
  probing of large language models. Contains 1,019 CC-Riddle-derived reference
  riddles with character structure cards, 600 model-authored riddles with
  quality-control verdicts, a 597-item generation-solving closed loop with
  cross-model blind test and same-item self-test, and a 24-item ICL control
  task (192 API calls). Released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 for the data, MIT for
  the scripts, CC BY 4.0 for the documentation. This is a diagnostic probe,
  not a ranking benchmark.
keywords:
  - Chinese character riddles
  - structural probe
  - large language models
  - behavioral probe
  - control task
  - generation-solving closed loop
  - in-context learning
  - dataset
repository-code: "https://github.com/SunSeeding/ccrp"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24077793"
# Zenodo version DOI for the published v0.1 deposit (2026-11-09).
# The concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24077792 resolves to all versions of this record.
# Citation and archiving notes: docs/ZENODO.md.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24077793"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "汉字字谜能否成为大语言模型的结构探针？"
  authors:
    - name: "Spring Buds Data Source Inc."
      alias: "春芽数源"
  year: 2026
  note: >-
    English translation: "Can Chinese Character Riddles Serve as Structural
    Probes for Large Language Models?". Both editions are included as
    paper/riddle-paper{,-en}.md, with typeset .html and .pdf editions.
    A second, independent paper was added on 2026-11-10; it is listed
    under references and must not be confused with this preferred citation.
# Two independent papers are associated with CCRP DataSet v0.1. Paper 2 is
# signed by a different research group and its Chinese original states no
# licence for the paper text itself; see paper/README.md. No DOI or URL is
# invented for either paper.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "汉字字谜能否成为大语言模型的结构探针？"
    authors:
      - name: "Spring Buds Data Source Inc."
        alias: "春芽数源"
    year: 2026
    note: >-
      Paper 1 (CC BY 4.0). Chinese original paper/riddle-paper.md and full
      English translation paper/riddle-paper-en.md, with typeset HTML/PDF.
      Adjudicates whether Chinese character riddles can serve as a structural
      probe: a conditional yes (diagnostic probe yes, ranking benchmark no,
      training-signal probe not yet decidable).
  - type: article
    title: "Blind Men Touching Characters: Probing Symbolic Algebra vs. 2D Spatial Perception in LLMs via Chinese Character Riddles"
    authors:
      - name: "Computational Linguistics and LLM Cognitive Diagnostics Research Group"
        alias: "计算语言学与大模型认知诊断课题组"
    year: 2026
    note: >-
      Paper 2. Chinese original (2026-11-06) archived as
      paper/gmn-paper-zh.pdf; full English translation (2026-11-10) at
      paper/gmn-paper-en.md with typeset HTML/PDF. Chinese title:
      盲人摸字：通过汉字字谜探查大模型的一维符号代数与二维空间失明.
      The Chinese original states no licence for the paper text; both editions
      are provided for reference and academic citation only.
